IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-art-28: Article 28 (Notifying authorities), Chapter III Section 4.
-- Article 28 is addressed to Member States and notifying authorities, that is, to officials. It is encoded here for what it decides
-- (layer 1). The seat layer has no seat for an official; paragraphs 8 and 9 mean something to a notified body and appear there.
-- Paragraphs 8 and 9 were inserted by the Omnibus (consolidated lines 540-544, marker `▼M1 INSERTED`): they have only the text as amended.
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first and answers NOTHING before Chapter III Section 4 applies (2 August 2025).
-- Every `FALSE-kind` comment on a bare "shall" not done marks a case-by-case choice (fork F-bare-shall in NOTES.md).

§ `Article 28: the parties and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 28 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 28 Member State`
    `Art 28 notifying authority`

DECLARE `Art 28 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 28(1) designate or establish at least one notifying authority`
    `Art 28(5) offer or provide an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform`
    `Art 28(5) offer or provide consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis`
    `Art 28(6) safeguard the confidentiality of the information obtained`
    `Art 28(8) ensure the single application and the unified assessment procedure`

§ `Article 28(1): at least one notifying authority`

-- src:532 | 1. Each Member State shall designate or establish at least one notifying authority responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring. Those procedures shall be developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States.
@ref Art 28(1) (src:532)
-- Gloss: every Member State must have at least one national authority that runs the assessment, designation, notification and monitoring of conformity assessment bodies, and those procedures are worked out together by the authorities of all Member States.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Member State has designated or established at least one notifying authority responsible for the procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the procedures have been developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1) the Member State has met the duty to designate or establish a notifying authority` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the Member State has designated or established at least one notifying authority responsible for the procedures`
        AND `the procedures have been developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each Member State shall designate or establish at least one notifying authority" and "Those procedures shall be developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show it breached.
-- src:532 | 1. Each Member State shall designate or establish at least one notifying authority responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring. Those procedures shall be developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States.
@ref Art 28(1) (src:532)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 28 party` `Art 28 act`
`Art 28(1) the duty of the Member State to designate or establish a notifying authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 28 Member State`
         MUST `Art 28(1) designate or establish at least one notifying authority`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 28(2): assessment and monitoring by a national accreditation body`

-- src:533 | 2. Member States may decide that the assessment and monitoring referred to in paragraph 1 is to be carried out by a national accreditation body within the meaning of, and in accordance with, Regulation (EC) No 765/2008.
@ref Art 28(2) (src:533)
-- Gloss: a Member State may leave the assessment and monitoring to its national accreditation body, if that body is one within Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 and acts in accordance with it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the body is a national accreditation body within the meaning of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment and monitoring are carried out in accordance with Regulation (EC) No 765/2008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(2) the Member State may decide that the assessment and monitoring are carried out by a national accreditation body` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the body is a national accreditation body within the meaning of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008` AND `the assessment and monitoring are carried out in accordance with Regulation (EC) No 765/2008`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the meaning of, and in accordance with, Regulation (EC) No 765/2008" (a power named by "may": fork F-28-2)

§ `Article 28(3): no conflict of interest`

-- src:534 | 3. Notifying authorities shall be established, organised and operated in such a way that no conflict of interest arises with conformity assessment bodies, and that the objectivity and impartiality of their activities are safeguarded.
@ref Art 28(3) (src:534)
-- Gloss: the authority must be set up and run so that it has no conflict of interest with the bodies it assesses, and so that its work is objective and impartial.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `no conflict of interest arises with conformity assessment bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objectivity and impartiality of the activities of the notifying authority are safeguarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(3) the notifying authority is established, organised and operated as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `no conflict of interest arises with conformity assessment bodies`
        AND `the objectivity and impartiality of the activities of the notifying authority are safeguarded`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be established, organised and operated in such a way that no conflict of interest arises with conformity assessment bodies, and that the objectivity and impartiality of their activities are safeguarded" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 28(4): different persons assess and decide`

-- src:535 | 4. Notifying authorities shall be organised in such a way that decisions relating to the notification of conformity assessment bodies are taken by competent persons different from those who carried out the assessment of those bodies.
@ref Art 28(4) (src:535)
-- Gloss: the people who decide on notifying a body must not be the people who assessed it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `decisions relating to the notification of conformity assessment bodies are taken by competent persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those persons are different from those who carried out the assessment of those bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(4) the notifying authority is organised as required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `decisions relating to the notification of conformity assessment bodies are taken by competent persons`
        AND `those persons are different from those who carried out the assessment of those bodies`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be organised in such a way that decisions relating to the notification of conformity assessment bodies are taken by competent persons different from those who carried out the assessment of those bodies" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 28(5): no activities of the bodies, no commercial consultancy`

-- src:536 | 5. Notifying authorities shall offer or provide neither any activities that conformity assessment bodies perform, nor any consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis.
@ref Art 28(5) (src:536)
-- Gloss: the authority must not do what the bodies do, and must not sell consultancy. The words "on a commercial or competitive basis" are read as qualifying the consultancy services only (fork F-28-5).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority offers or provides an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority offers or provides consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(5) the notifying authority has kept to the bar on offering or providing activities and consultancy` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   (NOT `the notifying authority offers or provides an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform`)
        AND (NOT `the notifying authority offers or provides consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall offer or provide neither any activities that conformity assessment bodies perform, nor any consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis" (a flat negative)

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: a trace in which the forbidden act occurs reaches BREACH.
-- src:536 | 5. Notifying authorities shall offer or provide neither any activities that conformity assessment bodies perform, nor any consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis.
@ref Art 28(5) (src:536)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 28 party` `Art 28 act`
`Art 28(5) the bar on the notifying authority offering or providing an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 28 notifying authority`
         SHANT `Art 28(5) offer or provide an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 28 notifying authority` BECAUSE "the notifying authority offered or provided an activity that conformity assessment bodies perform"

-- src:536 | 5. Notifying authorities shall offer or provide neither any activities that conformity assessment bodies perform, nor any consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis.
@ref Art 28(5) (src:536)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 28 party` `Art 28 act`
`Art 28(5) the bar on the notifying authority offering or providing consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 28 notifying authority`
         SHANT `Art 28(5) offer or provide consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 28 notifying authority` BECAUSE "the notifying authority offered or provided consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis"

§ `Article 28(6): confidentiality`

-- src:537 | 6. Notifying authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78.
@ref Art 28(6) (src:537)
-- Gloss: the authority must keep the information it obtains confidential, as Article 78 requires. Article 78 is another part's: its answer is taken as an input (seam S-78).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority safeguards the confidentiality of the information that it obtains, in accordance with Article 78` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(6) the notifying authority has safeguarded the confidentiality of the information` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notifying authority safeguards the confidentiality of the information that it obtains, in accordance with Article 78`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notifying authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:537 | 6. Notifying authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78.
@ref Art 28(6) (src:537)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 28 party` `Art 28 act`
`Art 28(6) the duty of the notifying authority to safeguard the confidentiality of the information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 28 notifying authority`
         MUST `Art 28(6) safeguard the confidentiality of the information obtained`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 28(7): personnel`

-- src:538 | 7. Notifying authorities shall have an adequate number of competent personnel at their disposal for the proper performance of their tasks. Competent personnel shall have the necessary expertise, where applicable, for their function, in fields such as information technologies, AI and law, including the supervision of fundamental rights.
@ref Art 28(7) (src:538)
-- Gloss: enough competent staff to do the job properly; and where it applies to a function, the staff must have the expertise it calls for (the fields named, such as information technologies, AI and law, are examples, not a closed list).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has an adequate number of competent personnel at its disposal for the proper performance of its tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(7) first sentence the notifying authority has an adequate number of competent personnel` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notifying authority has an adequate number of competent personnel at its disposal for the proper performance of its tasks`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notifying authorities shall have an adequate number of competent personnel at their disposal for the proper performance of their tasks" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:538 | 7. Notifying authorities shall have an adequate number of competent personnel at their disposal for the proper performance of their tasks. Competent personnel shall have the necessary expertise, where applicable, for their function, in fields such as information technologies, AI and law, including the supervision of fundamental rights.
@ref Art 28(7) (src:538)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `expertise is applicable to the function of the competent personnel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent personnel have the necessary expertise for their function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(7) second sentence the competent personnel have the necessary expertise` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `expertise is applicable to the function of the competent personnel`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where applicable, for their function"; the fields "such as information technologies, AI and law" are a list not closed (includes) (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the competent personnel have the necessary expertise for their function`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Competent personnel shall have the necessary expertise, where applicable, for their function" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 28(8): a single application and a unified assessment (inserted by the Omnibus; text as amended only)`

-- Step 1: the text as amended, in its own function with no date and no gate (PLAN.md section 5, "the as-enacted branch can be dead").
-- The "where" in the first sentence and the "provided that" in the second limit the duty; when they are not met the duty does not arise (NOTHING: fork F-unmet-where).
-- src:540 | 8. Notifying authorities designated pursuant to this Regulation that are responsible for AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I shall ensure that the conformity assessment body that applies for designation both pursuant to this Regulation and the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I is provided with the possibility to submit a single application and undergoes a unified assessment procedure to be designated pursuant to this Regulation and Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, where the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such single application and unified assessment procedure. To that end, notifying authorities designated pursuant to this Regulation and those designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I shall cooperate in their assessments.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(8) first subparagraph (src:540)
-- Gloss: where the legislation allows it, a body that applies under this Regulation and under the product legislation of Section A of Annex I can make one application and go through one assessment, and the two kinds of authority work together on it.
GIVEN `the notifying authority designated pursuant to this Regulation is responsible for AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conformity assessment body applies for designation both pursuant to this Regulation and the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a single application and unified assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is provided with the possibility to submit a single application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body undergoes a unified assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authorities cooperate in their assessments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(8) as amended first subparagraph the notifying authority has ensured the single application and the unified assessment` MEANS
    IF     `the notifying authority designated pursuant to this Regulation is responsible for AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
       AND `the conformity assessment body applies for designation both pursuant to this Regulation and the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
       AND `the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a single application and unified assessment procedure`
    THEN JUST (   `the body is provided with the possibility to submit a single application`
              AND `the body undergoes a unified assessment procedure`
              AND `the notifying authorities cooperate in their assessments`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall ensure that the conformity assessment body ... is provided with the possibility to submit a single application and undergoes a unified assessment procedure" and "shall cooperate in their assessments" (a bare "shall" not done)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that are responsible for AI systems covered by ... Section A of Annex I", "that applies for designation both ...", "where the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such single application and unified assessment procedure" (fork F-unmet-where)

-- src:541 | The single application and the unified assessment procedure referred to in this paragraph shall also be made available to notified bodies already designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, when those notified bodies apply for designation pursuant to this Regulation, provided that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a procedure.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(8) second subparagraph (src:541)
-- Gloss: a notified body already designated under Section A product legislation gets the same single application and unified assessment when it applies under this Regulation, provided that legislation has such a procedure. The text does not say who must make them available (fork F-passive), so there is no regulative rule for it.
GIVEN `the body is a notified body already designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body applies for designation pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the single application and the unified assessment procedure are made available to the notified body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(8) as amended second subparagraph the single application and the unified assessment are made available to a notified body already designated` MEANS
    IF     `the body is a notified body already designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
       AND `the notified body applies for designation pursuant to this Regulation`
       AND `the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a procedure`
    THEN JUST `the single application and the unified assessment procedure are made available to the notified body`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall also be made available to notified bodies already designated" (a bare "shall" not done)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when those notified bodies apply for designation pursuant to this Regulation, provided that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides for such a procedure" (fork F-unmet-where)

-- src:542 | A conformity assessment body that is designated pursuant to more than one piece of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I shall have to apply only once to be designated pursuant to this Regulation. A designation pursuant to this Regulation shall be applicable for all Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I for which the conformity assessment body is designated.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(8) third subparagraph (src:542)
-- Gloss: a body designated under several pieces of Section A legislation applies once, and its designation under this Regulation then covers all of them.
GIVEN `the conformity assessment body is designated pursuant to more than one piece of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 28(8) as amended third subparagraph the number of times the body has to apply for designation pursuant to this Regulation` MEANS
    IF `the conformity assessment body is designated pursuant to more than one piece of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
    THEN JUST 1  -- "shall have to apply only once"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of a body designated pursuant to more than one piece of that legislation

-- src:542 | A conformity assessment body that is designated pursuant to more than one piece of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I shall have to apply only once to be designated pursuant to this Regulation. A designation pursuant to this Regulation shall be applicable for all Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I for which the conformity assessment body is designated.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(8) third subparagraph (src:542)
GIVEN `the body is designated pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation is listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is designated pursuant to that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(8) as amended third subparagraph the designation pursuant to this Regulation is applicable for the legislation` MEANS
    IF     `the body is designated pursuant to this Regulation`
       AND `the legislation is listed in Section A of Annex I`
       AND `the body is designated pursuant to that legislation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applicable for all Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I for which the conformity assessment body is designated"

-- src:543 | The single application and the unified assessment procedure shall avoid any unnecessary duplications, build on the existing procedures for designation in accordance with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I and ensure compliance with the requirements relating to notified bodies both in accordance with this Regulation and the relevant Union harmonisation legislation.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(8) fourth subparagraph (src:543)
-- Gloss: the single application and the unified assessment must avoid needless duplication, build on the existing designation procedures and secure compliance with both sets of requirements for notified bodies.
GIVEN `the single application and the unified assessment procedure avoid any unnecessary duplications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they build on the existing procedures for designation in accordance with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they ensure compliance with the requirements relating to notified bodies both in accordance with this Regulation and the relevant Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(8) as amended fourth subparagraph the single application and the unified assessment procedure are shaped as required` MEANS
        `the single application and the unified assessment procedure avoid any unnecessary duplications`
    AND `they build on the existing procedures for designation in accordance with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
    AND `they ensure compliance with the requirements relating to notified bodies both in accordance with this Regulation and the relevant Union harmonisation legislation`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall avoid any unnecessary duplications, build on the existing procedures ... and ensure compliance" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:544 | 9. A notifying authority that has been designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I is also the notifying authority for the application of the single application and unified assessment procedure referred to in paragraph 8, unless the Member State designates another notifying authority for this Regulation.
-- VERSION as amended
@ref Art 28(9) (src:544)
-- Gloss: the authority already designated for Section A product legislation is also the authority for the single application, unless the Member State names another one for this Regulation.
GIVEN `the notifying authority has been designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State designates another notifying authority for this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28(9) as amended the notifying authority is also the notifying authority for the single application and unified assessment procedure` MEANS
    IF NOT `the notifying authority has been designated pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of a notifying authority designated pursuant to that legislation
    ELSE JUST (NOT `the Member State designates another notifying authority for this Regulation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Member State designates another notifying authority for this Regulation"

